From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:06:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Soloud_Filehack_fread: an empty request reads nothing

stb_vorbis reads an Ogg page without segments as fread(data, 0, 1), and
the bytes read were divided by the element size of 0: a WavStream of an
Ogg file cut inside its first page crashed with an integer division by
zero. fread returns 0 for an empty request, so the file now fails to load.
---
 src/core/soloud_file.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud_file.cpp b/src/core/soloud_file.cpp
index 865bf3f..86f756e 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud_file.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud_file.cpp
@@ -257,6 +257,10 @@ extern "C"
 	int Soloud_Filehack_fread(void *dst, int s, int c, Soloud_Filehack *f)
 	{
 		SoLoud::File *fp = (SoLoud::File *)f;
+		// fread reads nothing for an empty request; stb_vorbis makes one for
+		// an Ogg page without segments.
+		if (s <= 0 || c <= 0)
+			return 0;
 		return fp->read((unsigned char*)dst, s*c) / s;
 
 	}
